x2: new module, the LI_X2 interface of an IRI-POI.

x2_ims_message(dests, xid, correlation, pdir, sdir, matched) reports the SIP
message at hand - as received, or in onsend_route as sent - as an IMSMessage
xIRI (3GPP TS 33.128 7.12.4.2.1) to the Destinations (MDF2s) of an X1 Task.
Which messages, for which Tasks, to which Destinations, stays with the
config, which holds what LI_X1 provisioned.

A request reported from a request route also has the replies the node makes
for it reported, the other way, through a TMCB_RESPONSE_OUT callback: tm runs
no route for a local reply (onsend_route only sees relayed ones), and a
REGISTER's 401 and 200 or a local error are the node's own.

The payload is a BER XIRIPayload of TS33128Payloads r19 version8 (Payload
Format 2), in an X2 PDU of ETSI TS 103 221-2 V1.10.1 (version 6), with the
conditional attributes TS 33.128 5.3.1/5.3.2 ask for: Sequence Number,
Timestamp, NFID and IPID (modparams), the source and destination address and
port of the SIP message, and the Matched Target Identifier. The Correlation
ID is the Task's, or one hashed from the Call-ID, which every IRI-POI the
dialog crosses comes to alike.

A worker only builds the PDU, in shared memory, and writes its address to a
pipe. A process of its own delivers it: it numbers it in its context (XID,
Correlation ID), keeps one connection per Destination, over TCP with the
Keepalives of TS 103 221-2 6.2.4 both ways, or UDP, and queues a Destination's
PDUs while it is down, up to dest_queue_size. A full queue, or a full pipe,
drops the xIRI and counts it; nothing blocks a SIP worker. RPC x2.list and
x2.stats show the Destinations and the drops.

Not done: the TLS profile of TS 103 221-2 6.2 (the connections are plain
TCP), the other IMS records (StartOfInterceptionForActiveIMSSession,
IMSCCUnavailable), and reporting a Destination's faults over X1.

The doc/x2.xml is not optional: src/modules/CMakeLists.txt returns from the
loop over INCLUDE_MODULES at the first module without one, and every module
after it is left out of the build without an error. Nor is the README made
from it (the x2_readme target): the install step fails without one.

