+1. Overview
+
+   This module is the LI_X2 interface of an IRI-POI in a SIP node: it
+   reports SIP messages as IMSMessage xIRI records (3GPP TS 33.128
+   7.12.4.2.1) to the MDF2, in X2 PDUs (ETSI TS 103 221-2).
+
+   The configuration decides which messages are intercepted, for which
+   Tasks (XIDs) and to which Destinations, from what LI_X1 provisioned.
+   The module encodes the xIRI, a BER XIRIPayload of the TS33128Payloads
+   ASN.1 (r19 version 8), with the Timestamp, Sequence Number, NFID, IPID,
+   address, port and Matched Target Identifier attributes, and delivers
+   it.
+
+   Delivery is done by a process of its own: a worker hands it the PDU and
+   goes on. It keeps a connection to each Destination, over TCP, sends the
+   Keepalives of ETSI TS 103 221-2 6.2.4 and answers those of the MDF, and
+   queues the PDUs of a Destination that is down until it is back, up to
+   dest_queue_size. A Destination may also be UDP, with a datagram per PDU
+   and no Keepalives.
+
+   The TLS profile of ETSI TS 103 221-2 6.2 is not implemented: the X2
+   connections are plain TCP, and must only cross the LI network.
+
+2. Dependencies
+
+   2.1. Kamailio Modules
+   2.2. External Libraries or Applications
+
+2.1. Kamailio Modules
+
+   The following modules must be loaded before this module:
+     * none.
+
+2.2. External Libraries or Applications
+
+   The following libraries or applications must be installed before
+   running Kamailio with this module loaded:
+     * none.
+
+3. Parameters
+
+   3.1. nfid (str)
+   3.2. ipid (str)
+   3.3. keepalive_interval (int)
+   3.4. keepalive_timeout (int)
+   3.5. connect_timeout (int)
+   3.6. reconnect_interval (int)
+   3.7. idle_timeout (int)
+   3.8. queue_size (int)
+   3.9. dest_queue_size (int)
+   3.10. max_destinations (int)
+   3.11. seq_lifetime (int)
+
+3.1. nfid (str)
+
+   Network Function ID (NFID) conditional attribute of every X2 PDU, which
+   3GPP TS 33.128 5.3.1 has identify the NF: its FQDN, for example. Not
+   sent when empty.
+
+   Default value is empty.
+
+   Example 1.1. Set nfid parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "nfid", "scscf.ims.example.org")
+...
+
+3.2. ipid (str)
+
+   Interception Point ID (IPID) conditional attribute of every X2 PDU: the
+   POI within the NF. Not sent when empty.
+
+   Default value is empty.
+
+   Example 1.2. Set ipid parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "ipid", "scscf-1")
+...
+
+3.3. keepalive_interval (int)
+
+   Seconds between the Keepalives sent on a TCP connection to a
+   Destination, TIME_P1 of ETSI TS 103 221-2 6.2.4. 0 sends none.
+
+   Default value is 60.
+
+   Example 1.3. Set keepalive_interval parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "keepalive_interval", 30)
+...
+
+3.4. keepalive_timeout (int)
+
+   Seconds a Keepalive may go unacknowledged before the connection is
+   closed and opened again, TIME_P2 of ETSI TS 103 221-2 6.2.4. Longer
+   than keepalive_interval.
+
+   Default value is 180.
+
+   Example 1.4. Set keepalive_timeout parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "keepalive_timeout", 90)
+...
+
+3.5. connect_timeout (int)
+
+   Seconds a TCP connection to a Destination may take to open.
+
+   Default value is 5.
+
+   Example 1.5. Set connect_timeout parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "connect_timeout", 2)
+...
+
+3.6. reconnect_interval (int)
+
+   Seconds between attempts to connect to a Destination that has PDUs
+   queued.
+
+   Default value is 5.
+
+   Example 1.6. Set reconnect_interval parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "reconnect_interval", 1)
+...
+
+3.7. idle_timeout (int)
+
+   Seconds after the last xIRI for a Destination after which its
+   connection is closed and its entry freed. 0 keeps it for good.
+
+   Default value is 600.
+
+   Example 1.7. Set idle_timeout parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "idle_timeout", 3600)
+...
+
+3.8. queue_size (int)
+
+   Octets of PDUs not sent yet, all Destinations together, above which an
+   xIRI is dropped instead of queued.
+
+   Default value is 16777216.
+
+   Example 1.8. Set queue_size parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "queue_size", 67108864)
+...
+
+3.9. dest_queue_size (int)
+
+   Octets of PDUs a Destination may have queued, while it is down or slow,
+   above which its PDUs are dropped.
+
+   Default value is 4194304.
+
+   Example 1.9. Set dest_queue_size parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "dest_queue_size", 16777216)
+...
+
+3.10. max_destinations (int)
+
+   Destinations delivered to at once.
+
+   Default value is 32.
+
+   Example 1.10. Set max_destinations parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "max_destinations", 8)
+...
+
+3.11. seq_lifetime (int)
+
+   Seconds a Sequence Number context (an XID and a Correlation ID) is kept
+   after its last PDU. One unused for longer starts again at 0.
+
+   Default value is 3600.
+
+   Example 1.11. Set seq_lifetime parameter
+...
+modparam("x2", "seq_lifetime", 86400)
+...
+
+4. Functions
+
+   4.1. x2_ims_message(dests, xid, correlation, pdir, sdir, matched)
+
+4.1.  x2_ims_message(dests, xid, correlation, pdir, sdir, matched)
+
+   Reports the SIP message at hand as an IMSMessage xIRI. In onsend_route
+   it is the message as it is sent, between the local socket and the next
+   hop; elsewhere the message as it was received.
+
+   Called from a request route with tm loaded, it also reports the replies
+   Kamailio itself makes for the request - a local reply, or the 408 of a
+   timeout - with the Payload Direction the other way (2 and 3 swapped).
+   No route sees those. Replies relayed from the next hop are left to the
+   config, which reports them as they come in.
+
+   On a socket bound to the wildcard address (0.0.0.0 or [::]) the local
+   end of the message is the address the kernel takes towards the peer.
+
+   The parameters, all strings that may hold variables:
+     * dests - the Destinations, up to 8, separated by spaces or commas,
+       each [tcp:|udp:]address:port, an IPv6 address in brackets. TCP when
+       no protocol is given.
+     * xid - the XID of the Task, or its ProductID when it has one, as a
+       UUID.
+     * correlation - the Correlation ID, decimal. Empty for one made from
+       the Call-ID, the same for every message of a dialog at every node
+       that reports it.
+     * pdir - the Payload Direction of ETSI TS 103 221-2 5.2.6: 1 unknown,
+       2 to the target, 3 from the target, 4 both, 5 not applicable.
+     * sdir - the SessionDirection of the record: 1 fromTarget, 2
+       toTarget, 3 combined, 4 indeterminate.
+     * matched - the Matched Target Identifier, as ETSI TS 103 221-2
+       5.3.18 has it, e.g. <sipUri>sip:alice@example.org</sipUri>. Not
+       sent when empty.
+
+   Returns 1 when the PDU is queued for delivery, -1 when it is not.
+
+   This function can be used from REQUEST_ROUTE, FAILURE_ROUTE,
+   ONREPLY_ROUTE, BRANCH_ROUTE and ONSEND_ROUTE.
+
+   Example 1.12. x2_ims_message usage
+...
+x2_ims_message("tcp:192.0.2.10:6000", "2b36a78b-b628-416d-bd22-404e68a0cd36",
+        "", "3", "1", "<sipUri>sip:alice@example.org</sipUri>");
+...
+
+5. RPC Commands
+
+   5.1. x2.list
+   5.2. x2.stats
+
+5.1.  x2.list
+
+   Lists the Destinations: state, PDUs queued, sent and dropped, and
+   connections made.
+
+   Example 1.13. x2.list usage
+...
+kamcmd x2.list
+...
+
+5.2.  x2.stats
+
+   The octets of PDUs not sent yet, and the PDUs dropped before they
+   reached a Destination's queue.
+
+   Example 1.14. x2.stats usage
+...
+kamcmd x2.stats
+...
