+			Default value is 16777216.
+		</emphasis>
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title>Set <varname>queue_size</varname> parameter</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+modparam("x2", "queue_size", 67108864)
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	<section id="x2.p.dest_queue_size">
+		<title><varname>dest_queue_size</varname> (int)</title>
+		<para>
+		Octets of PDUs a Destination may have queued, while it is down or slow, above which its PDUs are dropped.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		<emphasis>
+			Default value is 4194304.
+		</emphasis>
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title>Set <varname>dest_queue_size</varname> parameter</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+modparam("x2", "dest_queue_size", 16777216)
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	<section id="x2.p.max_destinations">
+		<title><varname>max_destinations</varname> (int)</title>
+		<para>
+		Destinations delivered to at once.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		<emphasis>
+			Default value is 32.
+		</emphasis>
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title>Set <varname>max_destinations</varname> parameter</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+modparam("x2", "max_destinations", 8)
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	<section id="x2.p.seq_lifetime">
+		<title><varname>seq_lifetime</varname> (int)</title>
+		<para>
+		Seconds a Sequence Number context (an XID and a Correlation ID) is kept after its last PDU. One unused for longer starts again at 0.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		<emphasis>
+			Default value is 3600.
+		</emphasis>
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title>Set <varname>seq_lifetime</varname> parameter</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+modparam("x2", "seq_lifetime", 86400)
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	</section>
+
+	<section>
+	<title>Functions</title>
+	<section id="x2.f.x2_ims_message">
+		<title>
+		<function moreinfo="none">x2_ims_message(dests, xid, correlation, pdir, sdir, matched)</function>
+		</title>
+		<para>
+		Reports the SIP message at hand as an IMSMessage xIRI. In
+		onsend_route it is the message as it is sent, between the local socket
+		and the next hop; elsewhere the message as it was received.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		Called from a request route with tm loaded, it also reports the
+		replies &kamailio; itself makes for the request - a local reply, or
+		the 408 of a timeout - with the Payload Direction the other way (2
+		and 3 swapped). No route sees those. Replies relayed from the next hop
+		are left to the config, which reports them as they come in.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		On a socket bound to the wildcard address (0.0.0.0 or [::]) the local
+		end of the message is the address the kernel takes towards the peer.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		The parameters, all strings that may hold variables:
+		</para>
+		<itemizedlist>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>dests</emphasis> - the Destinations, up to 8, separated
+			by spaces or commas, each [tcp:|udp:]address:port, an IPv6 address
+			in brackets. TCP when no protocol is given.
+		</para></listitem>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>xid</emphasis> - the XID of the Task, or its ProductID
+			when it has one, as a UUID.
+		</para></listitem>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>correlation</emphasis> - the Correlation ID, decimal.
+			Empty for one made from the Call-ID, the same for every message of
+			a dialog at every node that reports it.
+		</para></listitem>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>pdir</emphasis> - the Payload Direction of ETSI TS 103
+			221-2 5.2.6: 1 unknown, 2 to the target, 3 from the target, 4 both,
+			5 not applicable.
+		</para></listitem>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>sdir</emphasis> - the SessionDirection of the record: 1
+			fromTarget, 2 toTarget, 3 combined, 4 indeterminate.
+		</para></listitem>
+		<listitem><para>
+			<emphasis>matched</emphasis> - the Matched Target Identifier, as
+			ETSI TS 103 221-2 5.3.18 has it, e.g. &lt;sipUri&gt;sip:alice@example.org&lt;/sipUri&gt;.
+			Not sent when empty.
+		</para></listitem>
+		</itemizedlist>
+		<para>
+		Returns 1 when the PDU is queued for delivery, -1 when it is not.
+		</para>
+		<para>
+		This function can be used from REQUEST_ROUTE, FAILURE_ROUTE,
+		ONREPLY_ROUTE, BRANCH_ROUTE and ONSEND_ROUTE.
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title><function>x2_ims_message</function> usage</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+x2_ims_message("tcp:192.0.2.10:6000", "2b36a78b-b628-416d-bd22-404e68a0cd36",
+	"", "3", "1", "&lt;sipUri&gt;sip:alice@example.org&lt;/sipUri&gt;");
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	</section>
+
+	<section>
+	<title>RPC Commands</title>
+	<section id="x2.rpc.list">
+		<title>
+		<function moreinfo="none">x2.list</function>
+		</title>
+		<para>
+		Lists the Destinations: state, PDUs queued, sent and dropped, and
+		connections made.
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title><function>x2.list</function> usage</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+&kamcmd; x2.list
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	<section id="x2.rpc.stats">
+		<title>
+		<function moreinfo="none">x2.stats</function>
+		</title>
+		<para>
+		The octets of PDUs not sent yet, and the PDUs dropped before they
+		reached a Destination's queue.
+		</para>
+		<example>
+		<title><function>x2.stats</function> usage</title>
+		<programlisting format="linespecific">
+...
+&kamcmd; x2.stats
+...
+</programlisting>
+		</example>
+	</section>
+	</section>
+
+</chapter>
